      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "| Subject | Dashboard | The question it answers |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Overview | [Overview](/d/lpbot-overview) | What is the whole system doing now, and does anything need me? |\n| Agents | [Agents](/d/lpbot-agents) | What is each agent doing, how is it doing, and why did it decide that? |\n| Pools | [Pools: live](/d/lpbot-live) | What are the followed pools doing right now? |\n| Pools | [Pools: history](/d/lpbot-pool) | How has one pool behaved over its stored history? |\n| Runs | [Runs: experiments](/d/lpbot-runs) | Which experiments are there, and how did the runs of one do? |\n| Runs | [Runs: one run](/d/lpbot-run) | What happened in one run, and where did its result come from? |\n| Runs | [Runs: compare](/d/lpbot-compare) | How do chosen runs, or groups of runs, compare? |\n| Runs | [Runs: pool and range choice](/d/lpbot-zones) | What did a run see when it chose its pool and its ranges? |\n| System | [System: Reth internals](/d/lpbot-reth-node) | Reth's own detailed metrics |\n\nThe same menu sits at the top of every dashboard: **Overview**, **Agents**, and the **Pools**, **Runs** and **System** lists.\n\nTo act, on the node machine, in `~/lpbot`: `make status` checks the whole machine, `make agents` shows every agent with what is wrong, and `deploy/RUNBOOK.md` says what to do."
